# Placeholder for the real, gitignored `secrets.properties` (copy this file to that name and fill
# in a real value before making a release build).
#
# BACKUP_PASSPHRASE is the fixed secret the Settings > Your Data export/import feature derives its
# AES-256-GCM key from (see app/src/main/java/com/appricodes/lens_whisper/data/BackupCrypto.kt).
# It is baked into the APK as BuildConfig.BACKUP_PASSPHRASE, so it is *obfuscation of an exported
# file at rest*, not a secret safe against someone who has the APK — the export dialog's own legal
# notice says as much to the user. Its real job is to keep an exported .fdb from being a plain zip
# that any file manager opens by accident.
#
# Every build that should be able to read another build's .fdb files must use the same value here.
# A clone without a secrets.properties still compiles; it just uses the placeholder default in
# app/build.gradle.kts and cannot read a properly-keyed export.
BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=replace-me-with-a-long-random-string
